From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000002 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Jenkins <lukejenkins@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] mhi_uci: bind "ADB" channel to UCI chardev
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Second half of the ADB-over-MHI investigation patch series. Adds an
{ .chan = "ADB", .driver_data = 0x4000 } entry to the OOT pcie_mhi
driver's mhi_uci_match_table[] in devices/mhi_uci.c. With patch 0001
in place, the MHI core creates an mhi_dev with chan_name = "ADB"
when the modem firmware advertises channels 36/37; this entry binds
the UCI chardev driver to it, exposing /dev/mhi_ADB.

MTU is set to 0x4000 (16 KiB), matching SAHARA and EDL. The actual
ADB protocol frame size is unknown on this firmware family, but
16 KiB is safe for any sane framed protocol and easy to revisit
if testing reveals a different optimum.

Validated on Quectel RM520N-GL-AP (firmware R01A07_11.204.11.204) and
Foxconn T99W640 / Dell DW5934e (SDX72). Not submitted upstream.

Reference: README.md (ADB-over-MHI findings).
Signed-off-by: Luke Jenkins <lukejenkins@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 devices/mhi_uci.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/devices/mhi_uci.c	2026-04-17 18:43:50.669906442 +0000
+++ b/devices/mhi_uci.c	2026-04-17 18:43:46.692901419 +0000
@@ -916,6 +916,8 @@
 	{ .chan = "LOOPBACK", .driver_data = 0x1000 },
 	{ .chan = "SAHARA", .driver_data = 0x4000 },
 	{ .chan = "EDL", .driver_data = 0x4000 },
+	/* Quectel ADB fastboot/runtime channels (36/37) */
+	{ .chan = "ADB", .driver_data = 0x4000 },
 	{ .chan = "DIAG", .driver_data = DIAG_MAX_PCIE_PKT_SZ },
 	{ .chan = "MBIM", .driver_data = 0x1000 },
 	{ .chan = "QMI0", .driver_data = 0x1000 },
